# Semgrep path exclusions for the bedrock module scan (see the repository root's
# .semgrepignore for the same entries under their root-relative paths).
#
# bedrock renders Terraform, YAML and Markdown from text/template: html/template's contextual
# escaping would corrupt that output, so both renderers (the application's stack and the
# organization's foundation) are excluded from the text-template audit rather than marked
# inline. The GitHub test fake answers JSON to the client under
# test, so the direct-write audit (an HTML page writing user data) does not apply to it.
internal/render/render.go
internal/org/render.go
internal/github/githubtest/server.go
# The migration renumber runs git with the repository's own paths (the default branch's
# tree, the tracked files, git mv), which is its purpose; the dangerous-exec audit does
# not apply to it.
internal/migration/git.go
